## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-tenant observability with strict data isolation, covering tracing, logging, sampling, and validation.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry and trace propagation
- Tenant isolation and boundary enforcement
- Per-tenant sampling and data redaction
- Validation in a single-namespace scenario

## Code Example

```javascript
// PII redaction example (logs)
function redactLogEvent(event, tenantId) {
  const safe = {...event};
  if (safe.message) safe.message = safe.message.replace(/\b(email|ssn|password)\b[^:]*: [^,]+/gi, 'PII_REDACTED');
  if (safe.user && safe.user.id) safe.user.id = 'REDACTED';
  return safe;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and remediate cross-tenant leakage in traces?
- What metrics would you surface to confirm per-tenant isolation is preserved during incidents?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical design of end-to-end attestation workflows in multi-tenant environments with integrated policy enforcement and security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Post-deployment tenant-scoped attestations using HSM-based key management
- SBOM integrity verification and runtime hashing for supply chain security
- OPA/Gatekeeper integration for policy validation and traffic gating
- Multi-tenant security isolation with compliance enforcement mechanisms

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sample attestation verification pseudocode
function verifyAttestation(attestation, tenantPolicy) {
  // Validate signature with tenant's HSM public key
  const isValidSignature = crypto.verify(
    attestation.signature,
    attestation.payload,
    tenantPolicy.publicKey
  );

  // Check policy compliance through OPA/Gatekeeper
  const isCompliant = opa.evaluate(
    attestation.payload,
    tenantPolicy.constraints
  );

  return isValidSignature && isCompliant;
}
```
